<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I942ff694a237306eab60834c2cd5096775bfe8b8" commit="ec4e511c86d80945cc87a541808e6363c7313dc4" commit_message="tpm: spi: fix stopwatch implementation bug  Stopwatch expiration check was expiring immediately, this patch fixes the bug.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:50645 TEST=SPI TPM initialization does not fail any more.  Change-Id: I942ff694a237306eab60834c2cd5096775bfe8b8 Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/356591 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="356591" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/91/356591/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I72e288ab588bd51a24f58ae4b423304e2732a986" commit="e15cfcd30b67a43e15d2b31a73cda3fc87e3abf6" commit_message="tpm: disable excessive debug output  No need to pollute the console output TPM message dumps.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:50645 TEST=TPM dumps disappeared from depthcharge console log  Change-Id: I72e288ab588bd51a24f58ae4b423304e2732a986 Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/356592 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="356592" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/92/356592/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I148470c6d16a0cd6dd79654482589cb18954eff1" commit="cda0177eaa1b2b3ce9b0f9fd4bb13c7b8a157a5c" commit_message="FROMLIST: regulator: pwm: Fix regulator ramp delay for continuous mode  The original commit adding support for continuous voltage mode didn't handle the regulator ramp delay properly.  It treated the delay as a fixed delay in uS despite the property being defined as uV / uS.  Let's adjust it.  Luckily there appear to be no users of this ramp delay for PWM regulators (as per grepping through device trees in linuxnext).  Note also that the upper bound of usleep_range probably shouldn't be a full 1 ms longer than the lower bound since I've seen plenty of hardware with a ramp rate of ~5000 uS / uV and for small jumps the total delays are in the tens of uS.  1000 is way too much.  We'll try to be dynamic and use 10%  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54814 TEST=Reboots still stable  Change-Id: I148470c6d16a0cd6dd79654482589cb18954eff1 Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9201831/) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/356485 Reviewed-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="356485" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/85/356485/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3ca405567fad9e1f91b9b64770035f1719f5b165" commit="b12634437ceb7846c6469456cf757cb662de4f03" commit_message="Break down platform_ExternalUsbperipherals tests cases &amp; add to new suite: usb_detect  BUG=chromium:621966 TEST=None  Change-Id: I3ca405567fad9e1f91b9b64770035f1719f5b165 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/355720 Commit-Ready: Helen Zhang &lt;helenzhang@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Helen Zhang &lt;helenzhang@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Kalin Stoyanov &lt;kalin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="355720" owner_email="helenzhang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/20/355720/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8c0753f12899e9f203c04477ae520bcda40d5fd8" commit="65840368833081083ed86a71935de1abceed6836" commit_message="common: Decouple temp sensor from thermal throttling  Not everything with a temperature sensor uses thermal throttling. This change modifies the conditional build to enable building temp sensor source without thermal throttling.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=make buildall -j  Change-Id: I8c0753f12899e9f203c04477ae520bcda40d5fd8 Signed-off-by: Mary Ruthven &lt;mruthven@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/356484 Reviewed-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="356484" owner_email="mruthven@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/84/356484/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I192ba874f83b2f2dcf0caea8b6281942198cc382" commit="cc800fb816e8732e65020f1f54b03c2590728390" commit_message="Change touch FW noise test to 10Vpp  Our spec only requires touch devices to pass for electrical noise &lt;= 10Vpp, but we've been testing it at 20Vpp for good measure.  For the sake of simplicity and so we don't have to keep explaining why what's going on to people, we should just change it to 10Vpp.  It more obviously tests our spec that way.  BUG=chromium:620090 TEST=manually tested  Change-Id: I192ba874f83b2f2dcf0caea8b6281942198cc382 Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/356010 Reviewed-by: Shyh-In Hwang &lt;josephsih@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="356010" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/touch_firmware_test" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/touch_firmware_test" ref="refs/changes/10/356010/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="8514.0.0-rc2"/></manifest>